														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3854924">
									

<p>Related suggestion: based on the interview log, &quot;does not show any <em>inclination</em> to alter its routine&quot; is misleading. 1917 clearly wants to change what it's doing, it's just in a repeated state of believing that change will come tomorrow.</p>
<p>Changing this description to imply that 1917 is unable to change would give away the game far too early, though, so I would suggest something like &quot;maintains its own routine without the need for outside enforcement&quot;, or even &quot;has resisted all efforts to modify its routine&quot; if you're feeling sneaky. (The fact that it doesn't <em>consciously</em> resist can be saved for the reveal in the interview. :P)</p>
<p>Unrelated: I'm amused by how close this entry's number is to both <a href="/scp-1914">SCP-1914</a> and <a href="/scp-1915">SCP-1915</a>.</p>

							</div>

								
